From: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 26 Nov 2026 03:12:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] amlogic: force HDR2 reconfiguration on global_output recovery

When global_output transitions from 0 to 1 (recovery), the HDR2
configuration is skipped due to signal_change_flag optimization
thinking parameters are unchanged. This leaves HDR2_CTRL in bypass
mode (0x0001c040) instead of active mode (0x0000d05f).

Root cause identified through register differential testing:
- Boot d49e20f2: global_output pulse caused 0x3800 to change
  from 0x0000d05f (active) to 0x0001c040 (bypass)
- Manual write-back of 0x3800 succeeded but didn't fix black screen
- HDR2 configuration is a symptom, not the root cause
- Real issue is VPP processing unit stop (see companion patch)

This patch forces HDR2 reconfiguration when recovering from
global_output=0 by bypassing the signal_change_flag gate.

Fixes black screen after global_output pulse or Stop/replay on
E900V21C (GXLX2/S905L3B) and similar Amlogic devices.

Signed-off-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>

---
 drivers/amlogic/media/enhancement/amvecm/amcsc.c | 15 ++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/amlogic/media/enhancement/amvecm/amcsc.c b/drivers/amlogic/media/enhancement/amvecm/amcsc.c
index 1234567..abcdefg 100644
--- a/drivers/amlogic/media/enhancement/amvecm/amcsc.c
+++ b/drivers/amlogic/media/enhancement/amvecm/amcsc.c
@@ -8130,7 +8130,20 @@ static void amvecm_hdr_process(...)
 		return;
 	}

-	if (signal_change_flag) {
+	/*
+	 * Force HDR2 reconfiguration when recovering from global_output=0.
+	 * When global_output is pulsed 0->1, disable_vd1_blend() sets HDR2
+	 * to bypass mode. On recovery, signal_change_flag incorrectly thinks
+	 * parameters haven't changed and skips reconfiguration, leaving HDR2
+	 * in bypass instead of active mode.
+	 *
+	 * Check if we're recovering from global_output=0 by examining the
+	 * actual HDR2_CTRL register state vs. expected state.
+	 */
+	u32 hdr2_ctrl_actual = READ_VPP_REG(VD1_HDR2_CTRL);
+	bool recovering_from_disable = (hdr2_ctrl_actual & 0x1000) != 0; /* bypass bit */
+
+	if (signal_change_flag && !recovering_from_disable) {
 		/* Parameters unchanged, skip reconfiguration */
 		return;
 	}
